      "shortest": true,
      "solution": "# The number to test\nnum = input()\nfailed_conditions = []\n\nfor i in num:\n    if i == '0':\n        failed_conditions.append(1)\n        break  # No point continuing if there's a zero\n    if num.count(i) > 1:\n        if 2 not in failed_conditions:\n            failed_conditions.append(2)\n    if int(num) % int(i) != 0:\n        if 3 not in failed_conditions:\n            failed_conditions.append(3)\n\n# Result\nif not failed_conditions:\n    print(num, \"true\")\nelse:\n    print(num, \"false\")",
      "statement": "A positive integer is called digisible if it meets all three of the following conditions:\n\n1. No zero digits — None of its digits is 0.\n2. All digits are unique — No digit appears more than once.\n3. Divisible by each digit — The number is evenly divisible by every one of its digits.",
